   "definition_quote": "Suppose there are $C$ distinct contexts in the context set $\\mathcal{X}$, and the context at time $t$ is $x_t \\in \\{1, 2, ..., C\\}$. ... Define the policy set to be all the possible mappings from contexts to arms as $\\Pi = \\{f: \\mathcal{X} \\rightarrow \\mathcal{A}\\}$, then the regret of the agent is defined as: R_T = \\sup_{f\\in \\Pi} \\mathrm{E}[ \\sum_{t=1}^T(r_{t, f(x_t)} - r_{t, a_t}) ]"
  }
